    <node id="SUBJECTIVE COGNITIVE SYMPTOMS">
      <data key="d0">SUBJECTIVE COGNITIVE SYMPTOMS</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-reported cognitive complaints after infection. The text identifies individuals with subjective cognitive symptoms lasting more than one month after infection as a potentially more susceptible subgroup in which cognitive deficits may be more readily detected. | Self-reported cognitive complaints during the menopause transition, including brain fog and memory problems. These symptoms were more commonly reported by perimenopausal and postmenopausal participants than by premenopausal participants.</data>
