      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective sleep assessment used to derive sleep onset latency, sleep efficiency, NREM duration, and REM duration. | Objective sleep assessment method referenced in the article keywords and likely used to quantify sleep problems. | Polysomnography is proposed as a more direct and specific assessment of sleep parameters and sleep homeostasis, which would better account for the confounding effect of sleep pressure. | Objective sleep measurement approach rarely incorporated in the reviewed studies.</data>
