    <node id="PSYCHOLOGICAL STRESS">
      <data key="d0">PSYCHOLOGICAL STRESS</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Psychological stress is listed among factors relevant to post-COVID neurological manifestations and may independently contribute to or worsen neuropsychiatric and cognitive symptoms. | Mental health variable measured longitudinally in hospital staff during the COVID-19 pandemic. It is potentially relevant as a cognitive-outcome confounder, although the excerpt does not directly connect it to cognition. | Psychological stress is described as bidirectionally related to pulmonary health and capable of perpetuating distress; it may complicate attribution of post-infection symptoms solely to respiratory illness. | Mental-health condition characterizing the healthcare-worker cohort. In studies linking infection or occupational exposure to later cognitive or psychological outcomes, psychological distress could confound interpretation, although no cognitive outcome is reported in this excerpt. | Psychological distress is reported as increased during the initial phase of the COVID-19 pandemic in association with social isolation and lockdown measures. It is a broad mental-health factor that can confound assessment of infection-related cognitive or functional outcomes. | Mental health burden for which medical students are described as being at heightened risk. In studies of healthcare workers, psychological distress could confound self-reported or measured cognitive symptoms, although no cognitive outcome is directly reported in this excerpt. | General mental distress reported as elevated during the COVID-19 pandemic and relevant to prenatal mental health exposure pathways. | Psychological outcome mentioned in association with COVID-19 related stress exposure. Within cognitive-outcome research, psychological distress could plausibly confound self-reported or measured cognitive functioning, but the provided excerpt does not directly connect it to cognition. | Psychosocial stress is cited as an exposure investigated for its impact on pineal structure in male gerbils. | Stress exposure referenced as eliciting neural responses and inducing prefrontal cortical changes. | Psychological distress is presented as a mental-health factor that can precipitate or exacerbate somatic physical manifestations, complicating interpretation of physical well-being and COVID-19-like symptom reports. | A stress-related factor amplified by extended exposure to isolated, confined, and extreme environments. It may further contribute to neuroanatomical changes and may also complicate attribution of cognitive changes to the environment alone. | Stress exposure reported in the cited studies as regulating adult dentate gyrus neurogenesis and as the condition from which recovery is facilitated by environmental enrichment. | Mental-health disturbance reported as elevated during COVID-19 quarantine and compared with pre-pandemic epidemiological data in Italy. | A stress exposure associated with gender differences in neural responses. | A mental health-related state that older adults may experience in response to life stressors, potentially influencing depression-related outcomes and cognitive performance. | Psychological stress is referenced in a cited article on stress and health, including psychological, behavioral, and biological determinants. It may confound relationships between illness, social exposures, and mental or cognitive health outcomes. | Psychosocial stress was collected as a potential influencing factor for anxiety and depression. | Psychological distress is adjusted for in multivariable models because distress may independently influence cognitive test performance or cognitive symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.95</data>
      <data key="d4">338d5c8e-550b-436e-8de2-d7967ecb69eb_chunk_4</data>
      <data key="d5">338d5c8e-550b-436e-8de2-d7967ecb69eb,d134d8d2-15f1-4ff0-8200-7d5648814a90,78467a8e-f680-4a51-ab1e-3319fa63fbc4,38ae95af-7b69-4f7b-a1f0-e672a8f6c0c1,bc6b9304-2c43-48f3-9a0e-787398c896ae,ee75d849-2123-48c8-986c-64305968800f,3f321026-7152-49c7-8437-9d8bc137d2de,b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57,3b3e91e3-1658-4d23-b1ac-d599d49e418a,c25b6f4c-84d2-420a-96d3-e1e3b098131c,48d3bb41-1aa4-436d-9ee2-ae98f909777a,432eead5-bd19-425c-9c09-f7783e9ba546,58d74265-e619-4fb5-901a-b5a77919251b,fb8152f0-db86-4a24-bd62-ab9650b4159b,f4c249e6-968e-45aa-a5c0-98565cad65a3,a58fa766-b6ea-4602-9891-cd7e4997b3ac,fe2c70b3-e143-43f7-bbf4-4cdc081212c3</data>
      <data key="d6">PSYCHOLOGICAL DISTRESS,PSYCHOLOGICAL STRESS,PSYCHOSOCIAL STRESS</data>
