    <node id="DEMOGRAPHICS">
      <data key="d0">DEMOGRAPHICS</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Participant characteristics proposed for future study because they may influence engagement with online cognitive assessments in multiple sclerosis. | Participant demographic characteristics reported in supplementary data. Demographics can act as potential confounding variables in analyses of associations between SARS-CoV-2 infection, long Covid, and downstream traits. | Participant characteristics included as input features in machine-learning models for long COVID identification. These variables may influence associations between COVID-19 and longer-term outcomes, although no cognitive-specific association is reported. | Population characteristics cited as factors by which post-acute COVID-19 burden is analyzed. Demographic differences may influence observed PASC burden. | Baseline participant characteristics measured before ED work and considered among predictors or adjustment factors for later intrusions. | Participant demographic variables included with microbial abundances in the linear mixed effect models. | Patient demographic characteristics referenced as factors whose impact on 60-day mortality was compared in ICU patients with COVID-19, sepsis, and acute respiratory distress syndrome. | Covariate category adjusted for in linear regression models estimating infection-cognition associations.</data>
