      <data key="d2">Cognitive domain assessed by the Cognitron platform through computerised tasks involving linguistic processing. | A cognitive domain reported as contributing to underperformance and global accuracy deficits in the assessed Parkinson’s disease and REM sleep behavioural disorder groups. | School-age cognitive domain associated with white matter development changes. | A cognitive domain assessed using validated in-person measures in the post-COVID cohort. The excerpt states that language was assessed, but the visible findings do not report a language-specific trajectory. | A cognitive domain listed among the abilities assessed by the broader neuropsychological battery, although the excerpt does not specify a particular language test. | Domain-specific cognitive score assessed at HCAP and derived from the neuropsychological test battery. | Cognitive domain covering semantic fluency, phonemic fluency, and auditory responsive naming. | Cognitive domain involving verbal fluency, lexical retrieval, and semantic access. | RBANS cognitive domain assessing naming ability, verbal production, and semantic retrieval. | Mentioned alongside executive functioning in the title of a cited article. No neuropsychological test, effect size, respiratory-infection association, or follow-up timepoint is described in the excerpt. | Language was included among the assessed cognitive domains. It was not reported as significantly associated with COVID-19 history or acute-care site.</data>
