      <data key="d2">Pandemic-related restriction period described as producing major disruption to daily routines. In domain terms, lockdown exposure could confound associations among infection context, sleep, lifestyle, mental health, and potential cognitive outcomes. | Pandemic-related public health restrictions referenced in the cited studies in Italy, South Africa, and university students. These restrictions are relevant contextual factors because they were associated with changes in sleep, lifestyle behaviors, mood symptoms, insomnia, digital media use, and sense of time, rather than necessarily reflecting direct effects of SARS-CoV-2 infection.</data>
