    <node id="GAD">
      <data key="d0">GAD</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Anxiety-related measure or condition reflecting state anxiety and possibly trait anxiety; described as a competing factor affecting cognitive function and cognitive failure. | Generalized anxiety disorder is referenced as being indicated by a GAD-7 score of 10 or higher. It represents a diagnostic-level anxiety condition and may function as a confounding factor in analyses involving health status or symptom outcomes. | An anxiety-related psychiatric condition referenced through the cited GAD-7 article. In studies of respiratory infection and cognition, generalized anxiety or anxiety symptoms may influence attention, working memory, subjective cognitive complaints, sleep, and fatigue, making it a relevant potential confounding factor. | Generalized anxiety disorder, reported as a frequent probable mental disorder among surveyed healthcare workers. Anxiety may independently influence concentration, perceived cognition, and neuropsychological performance in cognition-focused studies. | Generalized anxiety disorder is referenced through the citation for the GAD-7, a brief assessment measure. Anxiety symptoms can affect concentration, working memory, perceived cognitive functioning, and test performance, making them relevant potential confounders in cognitive outcome analyses. | Generalized anxiety disorder is referenced in a study of polysomnographic sleep patterns in non-depressed, non-medicated children. It is a psychiatric condition that may influence sleep architecture and cognitive functioning. | Psychiatric disorder referenced in studies of amygdalar functional connectivity and gray matter abnormalities. It is domain-relevant as a possible confounder of cognitive outcomes because anxiety disorders can affect attention, executive function, and subjective cognition. | App delivery characteristic involving guidance or support, evaluated in relation to attrition. | Clinical anxiety condition examined in studies of polysomnographic sleep patterns and sleep architecture. | Anxiety disorder construct assessed by the cited GAD-7 instrument. Anxiety symptoms can influence attention, concentration, perceived cognitive function, and neuropsychological performance. | Anxiety-related condition explicitly mentioned in the study of the COVID-19 outbreak in China. Anxiety can affect sleep, attention, working memory, and cognitive complaints, making it a potential confounding factor in infection-cognition research.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.91</data>
      <data key="d4">b24179f1-ebda-47e4-9ae7-42c367d15e44_chunk_26</data>
      <data key="d5">b24179f1-ebda-47e4-9ae7-42c367d15e44,5e787f6f-1547-4d32-aa5f-4a0f4d841129,41fb90c0-1594-48bd-b974-39b7d20799d4,d134d8d2-15f1-4ff0-8200-7d5648814a90,46ccdeeb-683a-4650-9e07-68526b50880c,3b3e91e3-1658-4d23-b1ac-d599d49e418a,c25b6f4c-84d2-420a-96d3-e1e3b098131c,e21cc068-4de4-48f2-8c1b-ee2a8b6ef08b,65d2e8e3-6795-45dd-a0ac-fc33bf2597df,49cf3a6d-f9ae-40b3-a69d-cb2b9c6b11ee,2032fba9-e1ef-40e4-8be1-15076f27c7ff</data>
