    <node id="NORMAL AGING">
      <data key="d0">NORMAL AGING</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-infectious aging process associated with decline across multiple olfactory capacities, beginning around the fifth decade of life and becoming more prevalent in older groups. | Age-related cognitive change used as a comparator in the text. The observed cognitive profile in PD and RBD differed from normal ageing, because healthy older adults generally continue to improve word knowledge beyond age 50. | A baseline aging-related process against which imaging changes in subjective cognitive decline are described as extending beyond expected age-related change. | Age-related cognitive change mentioned as an alternative explanation for decline, although the authors state that clinically meaningful cognitive decline over a short interval is unlikely to reflect normal aging alone. | An aging-related comparison condition used to distinguish cognitive changes associated with amnestic mild cognitive impairment from expected age-related changes. | Age-related context that may influence brain hormone levels and cognitive outcomes.</data>
