      <data key="d0">STROOP TEST</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Neuropsychological test assessing selective attention, inhibitory control, and interference management. | Standard neuropsychological test included in the Stage 3 battery; commonly used to assess inhibitory control, interference resolution, and executive function. | A neuropsychological assessment mentioned as one of the specialized tests used to identify minimal hepatic encephalopathy. | Neuropsychological test explicitly cited in the article title 'The Stroop test: selective attention to colours and words,' commonly used to assess selective attention and executive control.</data>
