    <node id="HEALTH STATUS">
      <data key="d0">HEALTH STATUS</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">General health status is referenced through the SF-36 health questionnaire. Overall physical and mental health may influence fatigue, functioning, and cognitive test performance, making it a relevant contextual or confounding factor. | Health status is represented by the five-digit EQ-5D-5L score formed from five category scores. General health status may be relevant as a covariate or confounding factor when interpreting mental health or functional outcomes. | Potential covariate noted in the excerpt but not included in analyses because participant numbers were imbalanced across its conditions. | Baseline health-related factor identified as important for psychological distress during the COVID-19 pandemic. It may influence vulnerability to distress and other health outcomes. | A participant characteristic that may influence both subjective cognitive symptoms and objective cognitive performance. | General health-related variable cited as important for psychological distress during the COVID-19 pandemic. Health status may independently affect psychological symptoms and cognitive functioning, making it a relevant confounding factor. | Household-level socioeconomic factor evaluated as a control variable.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.72</data>
      <data key="d4">86f9ab26-f1be-4c98-8916-d978196e27f5_chunk_31</data>
      <data key="d5">86f9ab26-f1be-4c98-8916-d978196e27f5,5e787f6f-1547-4d32-aa5f-4a0f4d841129,9ac1c295-0116-47ef-a0b9-9e8531f02406,bc6b9304-2c43-48f3-9a0e-787398c896ae,a459cfaf-0077-4b3b-bd9e-1701c220e2a5,9187db96-dcf3-44df-84d0-501718447003,f4c249e6-968e-45aa-a5c0-98565cad65a3</data>
      <data key="d6">HEALTH STATUS,WEALTH STATUS</data>
