      <data key="d2">Disease-severity category referring to patients whose acute COVID-19 illness did not require hospitalization; used to contextualize cognitive impairment findings in a post-COVID-19 syndrome cohort. | Clinical-care/severity subgroup describing COVID-19 cases not requiring hospitalization; referenced in a cited study of persistent neurologic symptoms and cognitive dysfunction among long haulers. | Disease-severity or care-setting subgroup describing COVID-19 cases that did not require hospitalization. The cited Graham et al. study specifically reports persistent neurologic symptoms and cognitive dysfunction in non-hospitalized COVID-19 long haulers. | Disease-severity descriptor for the Long COVID participants, who were reported as not hospitalised during their acute COVID-19 infection. | Less severe COVID-19 subgroup that did not require hospitalization; still reported to show significant cognitive test alterations after recovery. | Milder COVID-19 severity category used as a comparator against hospitalized COVID-19 patients in prior outcome studies. | Disease-severity subgroup referenced in the title 'Symptoms and risk factors for long COVID in non-hospitalized adults.' This indicates COVID-19 cases not requiring hospitalization, but the excerpt does not quantify severity-related differences or cognitive outcomes. | Nonhospitalized COVID-19 describes the outpatient disease-severity category in the cited nirmatrelvir study of high-risk adults. The excerpt does not connect this severity category to cognitive outcomes or post-acute neuropsychological effects. | COVID-19 illness not requiring hospitalization; post-COVID neurocognitive symptoms and executive functioning deficits are described in non-hospitalized or never-hospitalized individuals. | Acute COVID-19 course not requiring hospitalization, cited as a context in which executive-functioning deficits were documented in young and middle-aged adults. | Disease-severity category explicitly mentioned in the phrase 'non-hospitalised patients with COVID-19,' indicating COVID-19 cases managed without hospital admission. No severity-stratified cognitive outcomes or effect sizes are provided in the excerpt. | COVID-19 severity/context explicitly referenced in a cited prospective cohort study of persisting symptoms after infection among individuals who were not hospitalized.</data>
