      <data key="d0">SDMT</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Symbol Digit Modalities Test, identified as one of the three cognitive tests most influential in explaining variability in the PACS sample's cognitive and mental-health data. | Neuropsychological test referenced as the Symbol Digit Modalities Test, used to assess rapid symbol-digit substitution and processing efficiency. | An established neuropsychological test used as the basis for the electronic Cognitive Reaction assessment. | A neuropsychological test used in the study to assess processing speed. | A standardized neuropsychological test included in the face-to-face assessment battery. It is commonly used to assess processing speed, attention, and visual-symbol substitution performance. | Abbreviation for the Symbol Digit Modalities Test, cited in the Spanish manual reference and used as a processing-speed measure. | A standardized neuropsychological test included in the HCAP battery, commonly used to assess processing speed; higher scores indicated better cognitive performance. | The Symbol Digit Modalities Test, used to measure processing speed. Scores were reported as standard deviations adjusted for age, gender, and education status according to the test manual. | A neuropsychological assessment cited as a bibliographic reference: A. Smith, “Symbol Digit Modalities Test,” Jun. 13, 2016, doi: 10.1037/t27513-000. The excerpt identifies the test but does not report study results, effect sizes, respiratory-infection associations, cohort details, or follow-up timing.</data>
