    <node id="COGNITIVE CONTROL">
      <data key="d0">COGNITIVE CONTROL</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Cognitive domain referenced in the cited model of insula function. | Executive-control-related cognitive domain included among the deficits observed in the described cluster. | A higher-level executive function discussed in relation to emotion, memory, and psychopathology. The dorsolateral prefrontal cortex is described as a well-recognized cognitive control region. | A higher-order cognitive domain mentioned as potentially impaired by thalamic dysfunction and also referenced as a target for more focused rehabilitation outcomes. | Executive cognitive domain involving control processes such as switching and inhibition; assessed by Switching Stroop and Trail Making. | Executive regulatory domain referenced through the cognitive control network; the text discusses neural connectivity within this network rather than direct neuropsychological test performance. | A cognitive domain used to define a proposed cognitive-control biotype among patients with major depressive disorder. | The ability to use task rules and contextual cues to guide behavior. In the AX-CPT, participants had to use the preceding cue to determine whether the target X required a response or should be ignored. | Cognitive regulatory capacity mentioned as linked to individual differences in reappraisal ability. | A higher-order cognitive function supported by working memory. The text links cognitive control to working memory as part of broader cognition. | Cognitive function potentially related to enhanced caudate-default mode network integration. No respiratory infection-related effect, test measure, or follow-up timepoint is provided.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.88</data>
      <data key="d4">516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_6,516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_40,516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_45,516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_60,516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_72,516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_73,516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_74</data>
