      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Overall cognitive screening domain assessed by the MoCA; relevant because MoCA performance remained in the normal range and significantly improved in the symptomatically improved group. | Broad cognitive functioning assessed with ACE-III. The sample mean ACE-III score was 92, and no significant differences were found by COVID-19 diagnosis, anosmia, or hospitalization requirement. | Overall cognitive functioning assessed in participants as part of cognitive status classification and cognitive screening procedures. | A broad cognitive outcome domain. The text states that structured exercise and healthier lifestyles are associated with improvements in global cognition. | An overall cognitive-performance domain reported to decline longitudinally in association with increasing plasma NfL levels. | Overall cognitive status or global cognitive performance, represented in the passage by the total MoCA score. | A broad form of cognitive assessment referenced as one possible objective measure of cognition whose use may contribute to discrepancies across menopause-cognition studies. | Broad cognitive functioning targeted by the screening and assessment tools discussed in the passage. The text focuses on culturally adapted or validated tools for assessing cognition in older adults and dementia/neurocognitive-disorder contexts in Iran and Egypt. | Overall cognitive functioning, reported as associated with performance on the visual paired associative learning task. | The broad cognitive domain measured by the MMSE. The text emphasizes that global cognition as measured by MMSE is not specifically linked to basal forebrain cholinergic neuron function or hippocampal function. | Cognitive construct assessed at the test level by the MMSE. Participants with prior hospital-treated infection showed poorer MMSE performance. | A broad cognitive outcome that improved more in participants receiving active home-based transcranial photobiomodulation than in those receiving sham treatment. | Overall cognitive status considered as a model covariate through MoCA score. | Cognitive domain assessed as part of the neuropsychological evaluation in the study. | Overall cognitive performance represented by the RBANS global score derived from the battery.</data>
