    <node id="1 YEAR">
      <data key="d0">1 YEAR</data>
      <data key="d1">FOLLOW_UP_TIMEPOINT</data>
      <data key="d2">The longitudinal follow-up period over which a French cohort analyzed the course of 53 symptoms after SARS-CoV-2 infection in 968 patients. | Follow-up interval referenced in a related article title describing posthospitalization COVID-19 cognitive deficits at 1 year. | Follow-up timepoint at which global cognitive deficits are reported in posthospitalization COVID-19. | Follow-up timepoint at which posthospitalization COVID-19 cognitive deficits are described in a related article title. | Follow-up timepoint referenced in a related article title on posthospitalization COVID-19 cognitive deficits. | Long-term follow-up timepoint mentioned in relation to persistent symptoms in adult patients after infection. | Long-term follow-up interval cited for vocational outcome after severe traumatic and non-traumatic pediatric brain injury. | Follow-up timepoint at which subjective cognitive deficit in new mothers and posthospitalization COVID-19 global cognitive deficits are referenced in cited studies. | Follow-up timepoint at which altered network topology and centrality metrics were reported compared with baseline. | Approximate age at which learning, memory, and visuospatial abilities were assessed in relation to head circumference at birth.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.86</data>
      <data key="d4">86f9ab26-f1be-4c98-8916-d978196e27f5_chunk_3</data>
