    <node id="OLFACTORY IDENTIFICATION PERFORMANCE">
      <data key="d0">OLFACTORY IDENTIFICATION PERFORMANCE</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Olfactory identification performance refers to the ability to identify odors, assessed by OPID9, OPID9noguess, OPID18, and OPID18noguess. Several odor identification scores declined with age and contributed to differences across cognitive-status groups. | An olfactory task/domain reduced in early Parkinson’s disease due to involvement of the olfactory bulb, contributing to general olfactory impairment.</data>
