    <node id="SGFAP">
      <data key="d0">SGFAP</data>
      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">Serum glial fibrillary acidic protein, used here as a blood biomarker of astrocytic injury; levels were higher in cognitively impaired COVID-19 patients and decreased at follow-up while remaining higher than healthy controls. | Serum glial fibrillary acidic protein concentration, abbreviated sGFAP, was measured in COVID-19 patients at T0 and T1 and in healthy control samples using the Quanterix Simoa Neurology 2-Plex B assay. It is treated here as a biological marker related to astroglial activation or injury rather than as a cognitive outcome.</data>
