    <node id="MEMORY LOSS">
      <data key="d0">MEMORY LOSS</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Cognitive symptom involving impaired memory. It is described as a long COVID symptom, a continuous problem in younger individuals infected with Omicron, and one of the symptoms compared between hospitalized and nonhospitalized patients 2 years after acute infection. | Neuropsychiatric long COVID manifestation involving impaired memory function. | A post-COVID cognitive complaint mentioned in association with gray matter volume changes in brain regions including the hippocampus and cingulate gyrus. | Cognitive symptom reported in post-acute COVID-19 syndrome; patients with memory loss showed different gut microbiota compositions in a prospective cohort study. | A specific cognitive symptom reported at long-term follow-up after SARS-CoV-2 infection and quantified in the meta-analysis of studies with at least 12 months of follow-up. | Impaired persistence or retention of memory, highlighted in the context of neurodegenerative conditions such as Alzheimer's disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.95</data>
      <data key="d4">5e787f6f-1547-4d32-aa5f-4a0f4d841129_chunk_21</data>
