s to post-COVID-19 condition, long COVID, persistent symptoms, sequelae groups, and long-term health problems following COVID-19. | Post-acute phase after COVID-19 infection, reflected by references to 'Long-COVID,' 'post-COVID health complications,' and COVID-19 survivors with persistent symptoms. This captures the follow-up context rather than treating Long-COVID itself as a respiratory infection. | Time period after acute COVID-19 infection during which cognitive dysfunction and neurocognitive symptoms are described. | Time after acute COVID-19 or after COVID-related hospitalization, when prolonged respiratory symptoms and appetite-related complaints may continue to be observed. | Post-infection assessment period in which respondents reported reduced self-rated health and post-COVID symptoms. The exact duration since infection is not specified. | Time period after COVID-19 infection during which self-rated health, PTSD symptoms, irritability, and cognitive recovery concerns are discussed. | Relative observation period indicated by the phrase 'after Covid-19.' The excerpt does not specify an exact duration after infection. | Follow-up timing implied by the phrase 'after COVID-19 infection.' The exact interval is not specified, but it indicates cognitive assessment occurred after the acute infection. | Unspecified period after acute Covid illness during which patients were assessed. The citation does not provide a precise follow-up interval. | Post-acute period after COVID-19 infection during which cognitive outcomes, especially executive dysfunction, are discussed.</data>
