    <node id="DEPRESSIVE SYMPTOM SEVERITY">
      <data key="d0">DEPRESSIVE SYMPTOM SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d1">DISEASE_SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d2">Severity of depressive symptoms reported during the COVID-19 pandemic; negatively associated with cingulum fiber density and cross-section in females. | Severity of depressive clinical symptoms following repeated traumatic exposure. The text reports that low cognitive flexibility is associated with a positive relationship between traumatic exposure and depression symptoms. | The level of depressive symptoms. The text states that more severe depressive symptoms are associated with increased concurrent suicidal ideation, and that treatment-related improvement of depressive symptoms in StD may be underpinned by brain network characteristics. | Severity of depressive symptoms, referenced across topics on antidepressant mechanisms and developmental trajectories. | The severity of depressive symptoms, discussed as an outcome related to perceived stress and its neural markers. | Symptom severity in late-life depression is mentioned in the cited Bambuí cohort study. It represents the severity level of depressive illness and may influence mortality risk and the degree of cognitive or functional impairment associated with depression. | Severity of depressive symptoms referenced through the PHQ-9 citation and studies relating depressive symptoms to reward-related neural responses. | Participants lost to follow-up had higher CDSS scores, indicating greater depressive symptom severity. | The severity of depressive symptoms, considered as an outcome potentially associated with GMV and perceived stress. | Severity of depression-related symptoms; the outcome predicted by right orbitofrontal cortex gray matter volume through perceived stress. | The adverse mental-health outcome discussed in relation to subjective relative deprivation, income rank, income loss, and CET policy implementation. | Severity or manifestation of depressive disorders and depression symptoms discussed as the main mental-health outcome affected by social transition, CET policy, memory deficits, and combined macro- and micro-level stressors. | Severity of depressive symptomatology, ranging from no depressive symptoms to severe depressive symptoms as quantified by the 21-item BDI. | Severity of depressive symptoms assessed in studies of Lactobacillus plantarum formulations, including single-strain and multistrain probiotic preparations. | Severity of depressive symptoms used as an outcome in meta-analyses of digital mental health interventions. | Severity of depressive symptoms, reported as associated with larger neural circuitry and improved following amygdala-targeted real-time fMRI neurofeedback in MDD patients. | Broad range of depressive symptom burden assessed in adults in Study 2. | Normalized depression scores collected after trauma exposure as part of adverse post-traumatic neuropsychiatric sequelae assessment. | Severity of depressive symptoms after trauma; modeled in association with gut microbiome characteristics. | Severity of depressive internalizing symptoms that has been prospectively linked to reduced sleep duration and other sleep-related problems. | Level or intensity of depressive symptoms examined in association with cognitive emotion regulation strategies. | Severity of depressive symptoms as reflected by the HAMD total score. The passage defines score categories as: below 8 points indicating normal or no depressive symptoms, 8–20 indicating possible depression, 21–35 indicating diagnosed depression, and above 35 indicating severe depression. | Level of depressive symptoms, including sadness-related outcomes, examined before and during lockdown.</data>
      <data key="d3">1.0</data>
      <data key="d4">e7fe57d5-6381-4c3f-b922-ec8893231f33_chunk_12</data>
      <data key="d5">e7fe57d5-6381-4c3f-b922-ec8893231f33,b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57,46ccdeeb-683a-4650-9e07-68526b50880c,9fd2d2b7-7479-41aa-88bf-84e0286f9506,c25b6f4c-84d2-420a-96d3-e1e3b098131c,d4be01b0-0472-4ae9-a366-e27372d7422c,8ce403aa-a9ab-4428-833e-1c72b8071f48,fb8152f0-db86-4a24-bd62-ab9650b4159b,f4c249e6-968e-45aa-a5c0-98565cad65a3,5e8deba7-6350-4d1f-9bea-c12bfb32945c,e21cc068-4de4-48f2-8c1b-ee2a8b6ef08b,ed93f40c-bf1d-4c99-b4e6-3ee0682b88c6,104e587b-e1a7-495c-92cb-cf76b7504b4c,65d2e8e3-6795-45dd-a0ac-fc33bf2597df,8fd1f72e-929f-457c-b76b-3655e2e4b342,a58fa766-b6ea-4602-9891-cd7e4997b3ac,2032fba9-e1ef-40e4-8be1-15076f27c7ff</data>
