subdomain or test is specified in the provided text. | Impaired cognitive performance reported in D-galactose-induced aging mice and described as improving after Lactobacillus paracasei PS23 intervention. | Broad cognitive impairment reported among COVID-19 patients in cited research by Qi et al.; described as relevant to the development and persistence of PTSD, without specific neuropsychological tests or effect sizes. | Impairments in cognitive functioning referenced in a cited remote digital assessment study, including deficits related to hippocampal atrophy in autoimmune limbic encephalitis. | Impairments in cognitive performance referenced across cited COVID-19 studies and used as the target phenomenon for identifying sensitive cognitive tasks. | Cognitive impairments in adults with schizophrenia described as a major contributor to poor functional outcomes and everyday functioning, and targeted by the online game-based training program. | Broad cognitive impairment construct mentioned in the cited review title 'Cognitive deficits in bipolar disorders: Implications for emotion.' The excerpt does not specify the affected subdomains, measurement instruments, magnitude of impairment, or relevance to respiratory infection. | A broad cognitive impairment construct mentioned in the topic title 'Cognitive Deficits and Working Memory in Schizophrenia.' | A broad cognitive outcome mentioned only in the title of the cited Kane et al. (2007) reference, which concerns identifying and monitoring cognitive deficits in clinical populations. The provided passage does not describe a respiratory infection, healthcare-worker cohort, disease severity, follow-up timepoint, or quantified cognitive effect. | Cognitive impairments in Alzheimer’s disease-related models, reported to be rescued following NSC-derived exosome administration. | General cognitive impairment outcome referenced in a COVID-19 hospitalized cohort, with acute-phase correlates examined. | Impairments in cognition reported in Alzheimer’s disease models and described as reversible after mitophagy enhancement. | Impairments in cognitive function observed in preclinical Alzheimer disease models after FSH-related triggering of pathology and neuroinflammation. | Broad cognitive outcome explicitly mentioned in the cited article title 'Neurovascular coupling impairment as a mechanism for cognitive deficits in COVID-19.' The text does not specify individual cognitive subdomains.</data>
