      <data key="d1">RESPIRATORY_INFECTION</data>
      <data key="d2">The initial acute COVID-19 episode used as the baseline reference for assessing long-term post-infection outcomes, including long COVID up to 2 years later. | Acute respiratory infection episode experienced by trial participants. Symptoms during the acute episode included sore throat, fatigue, cough, and phlegm, and symptom profiles did not significantly differ between comparison groups. | The acute phase of infection for which participants recalled symptoms at follow-up. These recalled acute-phase symptoms were identified as potentially subject to recall bias. | The initial acute SARS-CoV-2 infection after which long-COVID outcomes were characterized more than 6 months later.</data>
