    <node id="COPD">
      <data key="d0">COPD</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, specifically noted as an important example of pre-existing pulmonary disease. It may increase vulnerability to more severe respiratory illness and later sequelae. | Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease described as a pre-existing pulmonary condition that can independently contribute to cognitive impairment through hypoxemia, inflammation, and comorbidities, complicating attribution of cognitive deficits to COVID-19 alone. | Chronic respiratory disease referenced in a citation on depression, anxiety, and quality of life among COPD patients. COPD may confound functional, psychiatric, or cognitive outcome interpretation. | Respiratory comorbidity adjusted for in the post-COVID cognitive-functioning analysis.</data>
