      <data key="d2">Additional delayed memory task administered in Stage 2 alongside the 12-task C-MS battery. It was included because prior work showed sensitivity to subtle memory deficits in other populations. | Delayed object-memory task that showed medium-large differences between early-stage people with MS and controls, contributing to evidence of early object-memory impairment. | Delayed object-memory task; sex-related accuracy effect was -0.18 SD, age 80 was associated with a 1.05 SD increase in duration time, and education was not a statistically significant duration-time predictor for this task.</data>
