    <node id="ICU ADMISSION">
      <data key="d0">ICU ADMISSION</data>
      <data key="d1">DISEASE_SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d2">Marker of critical illness severity. The cited prospective multicenter study examines new physical, mental, and cognitive problems 1 year after ICU admission. | Marker of critical illness requiring intensive care; the text frames post-ICU impairments and their risk factors around admission to an ICU. | Intensive care category representing more severe acute COVID-19. Participants allocated to ICUs were reported to have a higher likelihood of long COVID symptoms than non-hospitalized individuals. | Indicator of severe acute COVID-19 illness used in the excerpt to define patients with greater acute disease severity. | Indicator of more severe acute COVID-19 illness. The text identifies prior ICU admission as a severity-related history associated with greater risk that pulmonary rehabilitation may trigger or worsen PTSD symptoms. | A severe clinical outcome included in binary logistic regression models assessing associations with infection status.</data>
