    <node id="PNEUMONIA">
      <data key="d0">PNEUMONIA</data>
      <data key="d1">RESPIRATORY_INFECTION</data>
      <data key="d2">Respiratory infection reported as related to two participant deaths during the study. | A respiratory infection cited as one of the single infections most often studied in relation to hospital-treated infection and poorer subsequent global cognitive function. | Respiratory disease comparator assessed through longitudinal imaging-derived phenotype group comparisons. Pneumonia showed some significant imaging-derived phenotype group differences, all in white matter, but these did not overlap with the SARS-CoV-2 imaging-derived phenotype findings. | A respiratory infection mentioned as an example of an incorrect diagnosis generated despite contradictory laboratory evidence.</data>
