    <node id="MEMORY PERFORMANCE">
      <data key="d0">MEMORY PERFORMANCE</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">A cognitive performance domain reviewed in relation to EEG alpha and theta oscillatory activity. | A cognitive domain identified as a coherent AS cluster comprising object- and word-recognition memory tasks across immediate and delayed recognition conditions. The memory measures clustered more by stimulus type, objects versus words, than by recognition timeframe. | A broad memory outcome reported to improve with neurofeedback in both healthy individuals and individuals with traumatic brain injury. | Memory functioning referenced in the review indicating that EEG alpha and theta oscillations reflect memory performance. | A cognitive outcome assessed in cognitively unimpaired Presenilin-1 E280A carriers and age-matched healthy non-carriers in the Alzheimer’s disease study. | Functional performance domain included in a multivariate association study with sleep quality, depressive symptoms, and grey matter volume. | Cognitive outcome domain examined in relation to EEG indicators, behavioral outcomes, and neurofeedback training intensity across three sessions. | A cognitive domain described as poorer among individuals with vasomotor symptoms of menopause.</data>
