      <data key="d0">MOTOR CONTROL TASK</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Task included in the C-MS battery to gauge visuomotor function; performance correlated with the less impaired hand on the Nine-Hole Peg Test, and no Stage 3 participants were classified as impaired on this task. | A task intended to assess Motor Control by manipulating difficulty through the distance between consecutive on-screen targets. Because it depends on screen geometry, it is sensitive to display-related variables that cannot be fully controlled in a web browser. | A task on which RBD patients showed superior performance compared with PD patients, relevant to motor execution and psychomotor control within the cognitive battery.</data>
