      <data key="d0">BROADBENT'S CFQ</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Broadbent's Cognitive Failures Questionnaire, a self-reported questionnaire assessing failures in perception, memory, and motor function. It contains 25 items scored from 0 to 4, has a maximum total score of 100, and higher scores indicate greater self-perceived cognitive impairment in daily life. A total score greater than 43 is described as indicative of significant cognitive complaints.</data>
