    <node id="PATIENT HEALTH QUESTIONNAIRE-9">
      <data key="d0">PATIENT HEALTH QUESTIONNAIRE-9</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">The Spanish version of the Patient Health Questionnaire-9, abbreviated PHQ-9, used to assess depressive symptoms. It consists of 9 items evaluating depressive symptoms experienced in the past two weeks according to DSM-IV criteria. | Patient Health Questionnaire scale used to quantify depressive symptom scores at 12, 18, and 24 months after acute COVID-19 infection. | Nine-item depression screening questionnaire referenced in a study evaluating its reliability and validity among patients with infertility. | Two-item depression screening questionnaire referenced alongside the PHQ-9 in a reliability and validity study involving patients with infertility. | Questionnaire instrument added to the dHS Covid Study to assess depressive symptoms. | Depression-screening questionnaire translated and validated in the Chinese population, with reported reliability, validity, and sensitivity in clinical settings. | Spanish version of the PHQ-8 used as a standardized screening instrument for probable major depressive disorder, with a sum-score cut-off of at least 10. It is a psychiatric screening scale rather than a cognitive test, but is included under the closest valid instrument category. | Four-item questionnaire used to obtain indicators of anxiety and depression symptoms. Elevated scores are interpreted as possible symptom indicators rather than formal diagnoses. | A 9-item self-report questionnaire, abbreviated PHQ-9, applied to measure depressive symptom severity. | Brief screening questionnaire, abbreviated PHQ-2, employed in the study to assess emotional distress or depressive symptoms. | PHQ-9 assessment used to quantify depression symptoms across participant groups. | Depression screening instrument referenced as PHQ-9 and compared with CES-D for measuring depression in Chinese patients with type 2 diabetes. | Patient Health Questionnaire versions used to assess depression outcomes in 12 trials. | A brief depression severity measure mainly used to assess depression symptoms. | Two-item depression screening instrument with summed scores ranging from 0 to 6. Scores of 3 or more are suggestive of a depressive disorder. | Brief questionnaire assessing depression and anxiety symptoms, relevant because recent untreated major depression was an exclusion criterion and potential cognitive confounder. | Questionnaire used to assess depressive symptoms as a factor associated with poor sleep quality. | PHQ-8; validated questionnaire used to assess depressive symptoms.</data>
