      <data key="d2">Participant classification based on liberal, fair, or conservative impairment thresholds: performance at least 1, 1.5, or 2 standard deviations below matched controls for accuracy metrics, or above matched controls for response-time metrics, across a specified proportion of tested metrics. | Classification assigned when participants scored at least 1.5 standard deviations from matched controls on at least 20% of measured parameters. | Comparator cognitive-status classification used alongside MCI in the consensus process. Participants could be classified as CU at subsequent visits even after an earlier MCI classification if follow-up review supported reversion.</data>
