      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">Biological developmental process reflected by fetal brain volume, cortical surface area, gyrification index, sulcal depth, white matter volume, hippocampal volume, cerebellar volume, and cortical gray matter volume. The text reports differences in these measures between pandemic and pre-pandemic cohorts and notes the known influence of gestational age. | Developmental brain trajectories in infancy, including total brain volume, surface area, cortical regions, fiber pathways, and functional connectivity. | Brain structure and connectivity at birth, including gray and white matter volumes, white matter integrity, and structural, diffusion, and resting-state imaging measures. | Developmental brain processes in the fetus that may be affected by placenta-derived extracellular vesicles and their miRNA cargo.</data>
