      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">A realistic to slightly unrealistically positive way of evaluating stressors; described as a proximal, modifiable resilience factor that mediates effects of protective factors and intervention-induced resilience improvements. | The PASS-process, reflecting a tendency to appraise difficult situations as more controllable or less impactful; proposed to support resilience and lower stress reactivity.</data>
