    <node id="COLOUR IDENTIFICATION">
      <data key="d0">COLOUR IDENTIFICATION</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Colour identification is the cognitive operation within the Stroop task in which participants must attend to colour-relevant stimulus information rather than automatically reading the word. | Olfactory identification performance; cases performed worse than controls, indicating persistent smell-related dysfunction after infection. | An olfactory assessment domain measured by the ABHT. Identification scores decreased with age and were lower in participants with mild cognitive impairment compared with cognitively normal and subjective cognitive complaint groups, independent of age, sex, and education. | Ability to identify substances by smell alone; the text notes that people are generally poor at this when cues from other sensory modalities, especially vision, are absent.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">516f7ce3-73d5-40bf-a988-9d3371580712_chunk_16</data>
