      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Remote, internet-based neuropsychological assessment tools described as feasible on commonly used personal devices without specialised personnel or equipment. The text emphasizes their role in reliable cognitive testing and wide-reaching participation. | Neuropsychological assessments administered online; the cited work focuses on factors that facilitate reliable test results in this format. | Remote neuropsychological assessment refers to cognitive testing delivered outside the clinic, including by desktop computer or smartphone. The text emphasizes the need for valid and reliable tools that can be administered frequently to detect subtle cognitive changes in cognitively unimpaired individuals. | Use of game-like or serious-game formats for neuropsychological or cognitive evaluation. | Performance-based cognitive assessment approach historically used to evaluate cancer-related cognitive impairment, noted as often failing to agree with patient-reported measures. | Detailed multidomain neuropsychological assessments are the cognitive testing approach used to evaluate both general and domain-specific cognition in the study.</data>
