    <node id="RACE AND ETHNICITY">
      <data key="d0">RACE AND ETHNICITY</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">People of color are identified as a marginalized population with historically reduced access to neurological care, making race and ethnicity relevant contextual factors in COVID-19 neurological health disparities. | Demographic factors implied by the description of a multi-ethnic elderly community sample and relevant to interpreting olfactory identification and mild cognitive impairment associations. | Demographic variables cited as factors contributing to differences in long COVID epidemiology across investigations. | Demographic factor referenced in a cited report on racial and ethnic disparities in prevalence of stress, worry, mental health conditions, and increased substance use among adults during the COVID-19 pandemic. | Sociodemographic factor referenced through Black-White differences in anxiety and depressive symptoms among older adults. | Matching factor used to pair controls 1:1 with qualified cases; partial ethnicity matches were accepted because of mixed ethnicities. | Demographic covariate noted as previously associated with APNS outcomes. | Race and ethnicity were analyzed using non-exclusive categories; participants reporting multiple identities were included in each reported category. No Device performance difference was detected by confidence interval overlap. | Population grouping factor represented by African and Caucasian people in the electrocardiographic comparison.</data>
