    <node id="COGNITIVE TESTS">
      <data key="d0">COGNITIVE TESTS</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Tests used to compare recovered suspected or confirmed COVID-19 individuals with matched non-COVID-19 subjects across multiple cognitive domains. | Unspecified cognitive tasks administered with EEG recording. The excerpt does not name specific validated neuropsychological instruments. | Unspecified cognitive tests administered as part of the study assessment battery, alongside questionnaires, physiological tests, and blood tests. | Tasks requiring sustained cognitive effort, cited as eliciting mental fatigue and impairing later physical task endurance. In this context, cognitive tasks are relevant because task duration and type may influence fatigue and performance outcomes. | Cognitive assessment tasks implemented for the study and used during data collection; the excerpt does not specify the individual task names or the cognitive domains assessed. | Set of neuropsychological task measures that generated summary scores for response accuracy and response latency and were included as the task factor in the ANOVA. | Neuropsychological assessments for which completion versus non-completion was evaluated; demographic features did not significantly differ between completers and non-completers. | Individual cognitive test measures used to assess baseline cognition and derive cognitive principal components. No single cognitive score differed significantly between controls and future cases at baseline. | Repeated neuropsychological assessments used to evaluate cognitive outcomes during the experimental cycles.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.76</data>
