      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Emotion regulation strategy use is referenced as a cognitive-affective domain studied alongside prefrontal cortical thickness and COVID-19 mental health. | Cognitive-emotional predictors including cognitive reappraisal and expressive suppression. | Cognitive and behavioral strategies for regulating emotional responses, reviewed across psychopathology. | Broad class of psychological strategies evaluated for their associations with anger, including avoidance, acceptance, distraction, reappraisal, rumination, and suppression. | General construct covering the habitual or spontaneous use of emotion regulation strategies, including acceptance, reappraisal, avoidance, distraction, rumination, and suppression. | Cognitive-affective strategies used to regulate emotions, examined in relation to psychopathology symptoms.</data>
