      <data key="d1">FOLLOW_UP_TIMEPOINT</data>
      <data key="d2">The second follow-up assessment time point, occurring 14 months after SARS-CoV-2 infection. | Post-infection timepoint at which long-lasting COVID-19 presentation is reported in about 5% of infected individuals. | Post-infection follow-up timepoint at which CFQ score and post-COVID cognitive failure were evaluated. | Post-infection window during which SARS-CoV-2-positive cases participated in the deCODE Health Study and underwent symptom reporting and objective cognitive and physical measurement. | Post-infection interval at which the C19Q symptom assessment and long Covid classification were performed. | A later post-infection follow-up timepoint at which the proportions of unrecovered cases and cases with persistent severe symptoms were lower than at five to six months. | Follow-up timepoint in the Australian primary-care surveillance study at which 35% of participants were unrecovered. | Follow-up timepoint in the Australian primary-care surveillance study at which 9% of participants were unrecovered.</data>
