    <node id="OXIDATIVE STRESS">
      <data key="d0">OXIDATIVE STRESS</data>
      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">Downstream biological process caused by persistent low-grade inflammation after COVID-19 hospitalization. It may contribute to tissue injury and broader post-acute sequelae. | Biochemical mechanism the trial aimed to explore in relation to persistent long COVID symptoms. | Pathophysiological mechanism associated with chronic respiratory diseases and hypothesized to contribute to neurodegeneration and cognitive decline. | Cellular stress mechanism referenced across psychiatric disorders, mood disorders, bipolar disorder models, and schizophrenia pathophysiology. | A biological mechanism listed among the health-related outcomes explored in prior research on air pollution and meteorological influences. | Persistent oxidative burden inferred from increased oxidation and possible compensatory antioxidant responses. | A biological stress pathway mentioned in external evidence on organophosphate-related lipid metabolism dysfunction. It may contribute to inflammation and mitochondrial impairment. | Cellular stress state involving oxidative damage, reported to be counteracted by heat shock-induced NSC-derived exosomes. | A downstream biological process described in the cited article title as being induced by chronic intermittent hypoxia in brain regions. It is a plausible neural injury pathway but is not linked here to specific cognitive domains, neuropsychological tests, or infection outcomes. | Biological mechanism mentioned in the title of a 2021 Biomolecules article on hyperbaric oxygen treatment and oxidative stress. The excerpt does not provide a direct relationship between oxidative stress and cognitive symptoms, long COVID outcomes, or healthcare-worker exposure.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.95</data>
      <data key="d4">c69cfb78-198c-48f8-b6ac-7bf289971093_chunk_7,c69cfb78-198c-48f8-b6ac-7bf289971093_chunk_47,c69cfb78-198c-48f8-b6ac-7bf289971093_chunk_65,c69cfb78-198c-48f8-b6ac-7bf289971093_chunk_66,c69cfb78-198c-48f8-b6ac-7bf289971093_chunk_137</data>
