      <data key="d2">Clinical subgroup of COVID-19 patients assessed after hospital discharge, indicating a previously hospitalized population in whom cognitive impairments were examined. | Post-acute hospitalized COVID-19 survivor subgroup. The passage concerns patients infected with COVID-19 who were treated in hospital and later discharged, representing a more severe clinical category than non-hospitalized infection. | Patient context indicating individuals infected with COVID-19 who had been discharged from hospital. This captures the post-hospital discharge populations referenced in studies of gastrointestinal sequelae, CT findings, mental illness risk factors, and clinical sequelae. | Clinical outcome mentioned alongside mortality in a study on personalized survival models for COVID-19 patients. It reflects patient trajectory or recovery status rather than a cognitive outcome.</data>
