      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">Event-related potentials are mentioned in the title of an integrative review concerning emotion and emotion regulation. They are electrophysiological neural responses that can index cognitive-affective processing. | Time-locked EEG-derived electrical potentials elicited by events such as visual stimuli or motor responses; used to reveal neural correlates of sensory and cognitive processes with millisecond-level temporal resolution. | An attention-dependent neurophysiological event-related potential discussed as a correlate of cognitive performance in Alzheimer’s disease and dementia studies. | An event-related potential component measured at Fz and Cz electrodes within a 300–600 ms post-target window in the AX-CPT task. The excerpt defines the measurement window but does not report group differences or effect sizes.</data>
