      <data key="d1">OCCUPATIONAL_EXPOSURE</data>
      <data key="d2">Occupational context mentioned as relevant because essential workers, like patients, could benefit from early neuropsychological testing to evaluate post-hospitalization impairment and its impact on return to everyday activities. | Occupational role overrepresented among Black, Latino and Indigenous people and associated with increased vulnerability to COVID-19 due to workplace exposure and limited protections. | Essential worker status is a work-related exposure associated with increased drunkenness in the remitted-abstinent AUD group, particularly among women in that subgroup. | Essential workers are identified as one of the occupationally defined populations included in the COVID-19-era mental health app trial. The excerpt does not specify that they were healthcare workers and does not link this group to measured cognitive outcomes, respiratory infection outcomes, or effect sizes.</data>
