    <node id="SET-SHIFTING">
      <data key="d0">SET-SHIFTING</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Executive-function subdomain assessed by the IFS-Ch, reflecting cognitive flexibility and the ability to switch between rules, tasks, or mental sets. | An executive-function domain involving the ability to alternate flexibly between tasks, rules, or response sets. It is commonly assessed by the Trail Making Test, especially its alternating-sequence component. | An executive-control ability involving shifting between task rules or cognitive sets, cited among Parkinson’s disease-associated deficits. | An executive-function subdomain involving cognitive flexibility, reported as impaired in adolescents with depression and recent suicide attempts and measured using the Wisconsin Card Sorting Test. | A cognitive domain assessed using the Wisconsin Card Sorting Test, referring to cognitive flexibility and switching between rules or strategies. | An executive-function-like cognitive domain previously shown to be impaired after androgen deprivation treatment in rats and assessed in the present work, particularly in older rats.</data>
