y need to be considered as a covariate in normative interpretation of cognitive assessment results. | Baseline demographic factor compared between participants with and without cognitive decline at 3 months; distribution differed significantly, with more females in the cognitive decline group. | Gender was used as a grouping variable for analysis of CSF estrone and estradiol detectability and concentration categories. | A demographic adjustment factor used when interpreting SDMT standard deviations, as specified in the test manual. | Demographic variable collected during baseline assessment and potentially relevant to patient-reported outcomes. | Participant sex or gender considered in comparisons of health status among imprisoned adults, with females reported to have more mental health issues than males. | Participant demographic characteristic reported for the sample; most participants were female students.</data>
