      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Neuropsychological subtest included in the cognitive assessment battery; raw performance was transformed into an age- and education-adjusted scalar score for classifying cognitive performance. | Standard neuropsychological test included in the Stage 3 battery; commonly used to assess attention, processing speed, sequencing, and executive set shifting. | A neuropsychological test added to the in-person assessment set because the C-MS battery includes a Trail Making task that is a computerized adaptation of it. | One of the three most commonly used neuropsychological tests in the MENA region. The text states that it was frequently used without appropriate cultural or linguistic modification. | Neuropsychological test added starting in August 2017, first in a subset of participants and then in the full cohort. It assessed speed and executive function, specifically cognitive flexibility, and is listed for 318 internal participants, 299 shared participants, 1107 internal visits, and 1047 shared visits.</data>
