atients. | Follow-up timepoint for assessment of symptom, disability, and financial trajectories among patients hospitalized for COVID-19. No cognitive outcome is explicitly described at this timepoint in the provided text. | Time period referenced in the cited study 'Characterizing long COVID in an international cohort: 7 months of symptoms and their impact.' The excerpt indicates symptom characterization at this duration but does not specify cognitive outcomes. | A follow-up duration referenced in a prior international long-COVID cohort study characterizing symptoms and their impact several months after COVID-19. | One follow-up stage included in the models as part of adjustment for stage of follow-up. | Infant age at which visual-system structure and connectivity findings were reported. | Infant follow-up timepoint at which head circumference was positively correlated with Bayley developmental domains. | Follow-up duration in an international long COVID cohort characterizing persistent symptoms and their impact.</data>
