    <node id="BASELINE">
      <data key="d0">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d1">FOLLOW_UP_TIMEPOINT</data>
      <data key="d2">Initial study assessment time point, including structured anamnesis, neurological examination, and psychometric assessment for in-person participants. | Initial study visit at inclusion, when the neuropsychological assessment battery was administered and MRI scanning was performed. | Initial timepoint of the prospective observational cohort study. Baseline procedures included online questionnaires, neuropsychological assessment, neurological examination, structural brain MRI, blood collection, and 18-FDG-PET brain imaging across two visits. | Initial assessment timepoint in a longitudinal study of COVID-19 sequelae and immunity. | Initial assessment timepoint at which demographic, clinical, cognitive, depressive symptom, social support, and sarcopenia-related characteristics were measured and compared across groups. | Initial measurement point before intervention or later prospective follow-up. | Pre-exposure assessment timepoint before participants started ED work. Baseline measures included demographics, prior trauma, cognitive and emotional factors, and genetic polymorphisms. | Initial assessment point at recruitment into the Oxford Discovery Cohort, where clinical, demographic, MoCA, and MMSE measures were compared. | Reference point for mental-health trajectories. The recovered group is described as returning quickly to baseline after an initial increase in mental dysfunction. | The initial assessment timepoint before the game intervention, when no group differences in cognitive or clinical assessments were reported between the two patient groups. | The initial study measurement timepoint used for comparison with the study endpoint. | Baseline assessment timepoint for the CDR-SB. | Pre-mission reference timepoint used for comparisons. | Initial assessment timepoint before treatment; sociodemographic characteristics were balanced, while selected exploratory outcomes differed between arms. | Initial assessment timepoint included as a covariate in the mixed model and used for baseline participant characterization. | The pre-treatment assessment timepoint for OCD severity and cognitive control network activation. | Preoperative assessment timepoint used as the reference for postoperative neurocognitive, pain, and mood assessments. | Initial assessment timepoint at which controls and future SARS-CoV-2 cases were compared. The excerpt reports that imaging-derived phenotypes with significant longitudinal effects generally did not show significant binary baseline differences between groups. | The pre-intervention assessment timepoint used as the reference for evaluating change in cognitive outcomes. | The cross-sectional analyses characterized estrogen levels, CSF proteomics, brain MRI volumes, and cognitive eligibility measures at the baseline study visit. | Pre-treatment assessment timepoint used as the comparator for clinical, cognitive, and MRI outcomes. | The pre-stimulation assessment timepoint used as the reference for clinical and neuropsychological outcomes. | The initial study assessment timepoint at which RBANS was performed and participant demographic characteristics were summarized.</data>
