      <data key="d1">OCCUPATIONAL_EXPOSURE</data>
      <data key="d2">Occupational pandemic context for healthcare workers, including work during COVID-19 and exposure to pandemic-related stressors discussed in relation to mental health vulnerability. | Occupational context of providing healthcare during the COVID-19 pandemic, including pandemic-related pressures on health-care workers and the medical workforce. The text suggests relevance to mental health burden but does not quantify exposure intensity or link it to cognitive outcomes. | Occupational context in which healthcare workers and physicians were exposed to pandemic-related workload, infection risk, and outbreak conditions. This exposure context is relevant when interpreting mental health outcomes and potential downstream cognitive complaints. | Occupational context implied by the study of healthcare workers during the COVID-19 outbreak. This exposure may be relevant to infection-cognition research because frontline or outbreak-related work can be associated with stress, sleep disruption, infection risk, and psychological burden, although no direct cognitive outcome is reported in the excerpt.</data>
