    <node id="MULTIPLE COGNITIVE DOMAINS">
      <data key="d0">MULTIPLE COGNITIVE DOMAINS</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Broad set of cognitive domains in which individuals recovered from suspected or confirmed COVID-19 performed worse than matched non-COVID-19 subjects. | A broad set of cognitive abilities potentially stimulated by dual-task training through increased cognitive load and more diverse cognitive engagement. | Different areas of cognition that may be impaired together and reciprocally influence one another after acquired brain injury or disorder-of-consciousness recovery. | The online battery was designed to produce measures across several cognitive domains relevant to PD and RBD cognitive assessment. | General construct from the cited systematic review and meta-analysis on cognitive domains affected after COVID-19, indicating that more than one area of cognition may be involved. | Broad cognitive abilities assessed in more extensive neuropsychological batteries. The text emphasizes that adequate evaluation of NCDs requires capturing multiple domains rather than relying only on brief screening tools.</data>
