      <data key="d0">MENTAL HEALTH</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Mental-health status is the outcome domain mentioned in the cited COVID-19 pandemic and lockdown article. Because no dedicated mental-health outcome type is available, it is represented as a potential confounding factor for infection-related cognitive analyses. | Mental health status assessed online by the participant using anxiety and depression inventories; it may affect interpretation of subjective cognitive complaints and cognitive performance. | Psychological outcome co-assessed with cognition after SARS-CoV-2 infection; mental health status may influence cognitive performance or subjective cognitive complaints. | Mental health is cited in relation to sleep among women in jail. Mental health status may influence both sleep and cognitive complaints or performance, making it a potential confounding factor in cognition-related studies.</data>
