      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Cognitive domain assessed through verbal learning and recall tasks, including immediate and delayed performance on the CVLT-II. | Cognitive domain assessed through oral presentation of a 12-word list, immediate recall across repeated presentations, and delayed recall after a 30-minute interval. Higher z-scores indicate better performance. | Cognitive domain mentioned in relation to stress-related deficits associated with prefrontal cortical volume loss. | A cognitive domain mentioned in a cited study title reporting stress-related deficits in verbal learning and memory in association with prefrontal cortical volume loss. | The cognitive domain examined experimentally using contextual fear conditioning and cell type-specific myelination manipulations in mice. | A memory-related cognitive domain included in the adjusted longitudinal analyses. Scores for verbal learning and memory improved progressively through 42 months post-COVID.</data>
