      <data key="d0">COGNITIVE RESERVE</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Individual resilience-related factor mentioned in the keywords that may influence cognitive performance and interpretation of post-COVID cognitive impairment. | Cognitive reserve, defined as the brain's capacity to cope with pathological processes through pre-existing cognitive resources shaped by lifelong experiences. It may contribute to resilience against post-infectious cognitive impairment. | Baseline resilience or reserve-related factor identified as a predictor of post-COVID-19 mental processing speed and executive function.</data>
