      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL FACTORS</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Contextual or environmental factors reported as associated with cognitive function in older people. | Uncontrolled contextual factors in the participant's environment during remote testing that may influence responses and affect psychometric interpretation. | Environmental exposures or conditions described as relevant risk factors for dementia prevalence and cognitive health in the region. | Environmental influences are briefly mentioned as possible factors relevant to variation in health outcomes, though details are truncated in the provided text. | Environmental influences referenced as factors affecting immune traits. | Environmental factors are identified as influences on major depressive disorder and may affect disease presentation or intervention outcomes.</data>
