    <node id="SLEEP DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d0">SLEEP DEFICIENCY</data>
      <data key="d1">CONFOUNDING_FACTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">Insufficient sleep, including the observation that ISS astronauts regularly sleep less than the recommended 7-8 hours per day. It is cited as associated with degraded neurobehavioral functions and elevated stress. | Sleep quality-related measure assessed during the winter-over period and explored in relation to longitudinal gray matter volume changes. | Actigraphy-derived percentage defined in the text as sleep duration divided by time in bed. Lower sleep efficiency may indicate poorer sleep quality and is a plausible confounder or adjustment variable in downstream analyses.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
