    <node id="INSULIN RESISTANCE">
      <data key="d0">INSULIN RESISTANCE</data>
      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">A biological mechanism contributing to type 2 diabetes mellitus and chronic hyperglycemia. | Metabolic biological mechanism referenced as interacting with mood-disorder-related processes. | Metabolic dysfunction described as being ameliorated together with palmitate-induced apoptosis through AMPK activation and fatty acid oxidation. | A metabolic state characterized by reduced responsiveness to insulin. In this study, insulin resistance is the main biological exposure of interest and was quantified using HOMA-IR from fasting glucose and insulin samples.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.94</data>
