    <node id="INFLAMMATORY RESPONSE">
      <data key="d0">INFLAMMATORY RESPONSE</data>
      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">Proposed transient pathophysiological driver that may underlie lasting post-COVID symptoms, including potentially the cognitive component of the symptom cluster. | Broad immune response emphasized as significant in the mechanistic overlap between long COVID and ME/CFS and as potentially occurring in the nervous system. | A biological response cited as leading to neuronal death in the cerebral cortex of patients with COVID-19. | An inflammatory biological response cited in organophosphate-related external evidence and conceptually aligned with the hsCRP inflammatory biomarker finding. | Inflammation-related biological response induced by tris(1-chloro-2-propyl)phosphate exposure.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
