    <node id="T2 6-MONTH FOLLOW-UP">
      <data key="d0">T2 6-MONTH FOLLOW-UP</data>
      <data key="d1">FOLLOW_UP_TIMEPOINT</data>
      <data key="d2">Second follow-up assessment approximately 6 months after the index period, where intrusive memory characteristics and content were reported. | Follow-up assessment conducted six months after the baseline emergency department work assessment. | Eligibility criterion for the summarized post-acute SARS-CoV-2 sequelae studies, indicating assessment more than 6 months after infection. | Follow-up duration reported in the RHUMATOCHIK study of rheumatic manifestations associated with chikungunya virus infection. | Follow-up duration reported in a cited prospective longitudinal study of chikungunya virus-associated long-term arthralgia. | Follow-up duration in a cohort study of Q-fever patients assessing health status after the acute phase of illness. | Follow-up timepoint mentioned in the cited article evaluating a 4-day mindfulness-based intervention among Chinese incarcerated people.</data>
