      <data key="d1">FOLLOW_UP_TIMEPOINT</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-acute recovery period, including hospitalized patients recovering from COVID-19, during which objective cognitive deficits such as slowed processing speed are described. | Post-acute recovery state after COVID-19 in which cognitive deficits were evaluated relative to controls. | Post-acute recovery phase during which participants underwent cognitive screening, a decision-making task, and MRI evaluations. | Post-acute recovery context in which prior studies reported decision-making alterations after COVID-19; the excerpt does not provide an exact time since infection. | Post-acute recovery period referenced in the article title as the stage at which patients were described. Behavioral, functional, and structural brain alterations are reported in recovering patients, though the excerpt does not specify the exact duration after infection. | Post-acute recovery phase after COVID-19 infection during which pulmonary patients may face heightened risk of cognitive dysfunction and amplified PTSD symptoms. | A post-acute recovery status mentioned in the title of a cited study on cardiac involvement identified by magnetic resonance imaging in patients recovered from COVID-2019. | Post-acute recovery state referenced in a cited study assessing cognitive deficits among people who had recovered from COVID-19. | Post-acute recovery status used as the timing context for observing cognitive deficits after COVID-19 infection.</data>
