      <data key="d2">A cognitive domain described as commonly affected in multiple sclerosis-related cognitive deficits, referring to maintaining attention over time. | Attention-related cognitive domain referenced as part of the cognitive landscape examined in recovered COVID-19 patients. | A cognitive domain identified as the primary outcome in the study protocol and heavily stimulated by both rehabilitation treatments, either directly through specific exercises or indirectly through prolonged attention-demanding activities. | Cognitive domain involving continuous monitoring and detection of relevant visual information, represented by rapid visual information processing A′. | Ability to maintain attention over time; measured using Rapid Visual Information Processing. | Cognitive domain assessed in the AX-CPT. Both early and late chronotype groups showed higher accuracy at their circadian-preferred times, indicating enhanced sustained attention. | An attentional domain included among the functions assessed by the neuropsychological subtests and relevant to subtle PCC-related attentional deficits. | A cognitive demand required during the Bluegrass EEG Memory Paradigm, supporting successful maintenance and retrieval of task-relevant information.</data>
