      <data key="d1">BIOLOGICAL_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d2">Glial fibrillary acidic protein, a fluid biomarker of astrocytic injury; reported as elevated in some acute/subacute COVID-19 studies but normalized at follow-up, was normal in the current study, and was altered in only 4% in Boesl et al. | A proposed cross-disease biomarker of glial degeneration used to investigate CNS damage associated with SARS-CoV-2 infection. | GFAP is cited as a glial blood biomarker evaluated for diagnostic accuracy over time in trauma patients with and without mild traumatic brain injury. It may indicate glial injury or astrocytic response, but the excerpt does not directly associate it with COVID-19. | Type-III intermediate filament component of mature astrocytes and biomarker of astroglial activation during brain damage, CNS degeneration, or aging. | Glial fibrillary acidic protein, a blood-based biomarker evaluated as an individual and combined predictor of later dementia. | Astroglial injury-associated protein, also known as GFAP, referenced as a neurological biomarker in multiple cited studies.</data>
