      <data key="d2">Age-related cognitive decline is referenced as an outcome delayed by Lactobacillus paracasei PS23 in SAMP8 mice. The excerpt provides no neuropsychological test name or effect size. | Cognitive decline associated with aging, described in the cited article as indicative of underlying neuropathology. | Cognitive decline and dementia risk discussed in relation to education, socioeconomic status, living arrangements, and other protective or risk-modifying factors in the MENA region. | Cognitive deterioration associated with aging, referenced as an outcome potentially influenced by microbial-derived metabolites. | The cognitive outcome evaluated in young versus aged mice; MIA unexpectedly protected only aged females from age-related cognitive decline. | A longer-term potential cognitive outcome discussed through the possibility that SARS-CoV-2 infection might contribute over time to Alzheimer's disease or other forms of dementia. This is presented as a hypothesis rather than an observed outcome in the sample. | A decline in cognitive functioning associated with aging, characterized in the text by transient and early disruptions that may be targeted by real-time neurofeedback. | Severe cognitive decline outcome referenced through dementia incidence in postmenopausal women in the Women’s Health Initiative Memory Study.</data>
