    <node id="POST-COVID-19 CONDITION">
      <data key="d0">POST-COVID-19 CONDITION</data>
      <data key="d1">RESPIRATORY_INFECTION</data>
      <data key="d2">The post-infectious COVID-19 context in which cognitive impairment, domain-specific cognitive profiles, and modifiable factors affecting cognitive outcomes are being studied. | WHO-defined post-acute condition following COVID-19 cited in the references. It provides clinical context for persistent post-infectious manifestations, including possible neurological and cognitive consequences. | A post-infectious condition following COVID-19, mentioned as the population in studies where HBOT was associated with improved exercise-capacity outcomes. | COVID-associated post-infectious condition described in the cited trial titles as involving persistent symptoms and neurocognitive dysfunction after COVID-19. | Post-COVID condition is mentioned in the title of a 2024 Scientific Reports article on long-term outcomes after hyperbaric oxygen therapy. It is represented under the respiratory-infection category because it is a post-acute condition following COVID-19 infection; the excerpt does not provide specific cognitive domains, severity strata, healthcare-worker cohorts, or quantified effects. | Post-COVID illness term used in the cited article on neuroinflammation. It overlaps conceptually with long COVID and post-COVID-19 syndrome, but is retained because it appears as a distinct term in the excerpt.</data>
