      <data key="d0">VISUOCONSTRUCTIONAL IMPAIRMENT</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Specific cognitive deficit involving visuospatial constructional ability, reported in the cited literature following mild COVID-19. | Selective domain-specific cognitive deficit, also described as a visuoconstructive deficit, detected in a subset of adults after recovery from mild COVID-19. | Impairment in visual construction abilities highlighted as requiring more comprehensive assessment and follow-up to clarify symptom persistence and rehabilitation needs.</data>
