    <node id="PHQ-9">
      <data key="d0">PHQ-9</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROPSYCH_TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">Screening questionnaire completed during Session 1 to assess depressive symptoms. | PHQ-9 is a self-reported instrument used for screening, diagnosing, monitoring, and measuring depression severity. Items are rated from 0 to 3, total scores range from 0 to 27, and higher scores indicate more severe depression. | Questionnaire score obtained before and during the pandemic through iStopMM and used to assess depressive symptoms. | Patient Health Questionnaire-9, used to assess depressive symptom severity. The excerpt states total-score categories of 5–9 for mild, 10–14 for moderate, 15–19 for moderately severe, and at least 20 for severe depressive symptoms. | Nine-item Patient Health Questionnaire referenced as being compared with the PHQ-8 for diagnostic accuracy. It is a depression screening instrument and includes an item on suicidal thoughts, but the excerpt does not link it to cognitive outcomes. | Patient Health Questionnaire-9, cited as a tool used to identify or screen for major depressive disorder/depressive symptoms in adult patients in Spanish primary care centres. | The Patient Health Questionnaire-9 was used to measure depressive symptoms. Although it is primarily a depression screening questionnaire rather than a formal cognitive test, it includes a concentration-related item and therefore captures cognition-relevant symptom information. | A nine-item Patient Health Questionnaire depression screening instrument used as the comparator in Dr. Yin Wu's highly cited study on diagnostic accuracy equivalency with the PHQ-8. | The Patient Health Questionnaire-9 is cited in combination with the PHQ-2 for screening to detect major depression. It is relevant as a standardized depression symptom measure that can help account for mood-related confounding in cognitive outcome analyses. | Patient Health Questionnaire-9 used as a comparator instrument for assessing depression validity against CES-D. | Brief questionnaire measure used to assess depression symptom severity. | The 9-item Patient Health Questionnaire depression instrument, compared with CESD-10 and PROMIS Depression instruments. | Patient Health Questionnaire-9, referenced as a symptom questionnaire equated to the HADS depression subscale in patients with major depressive disorder. | Patient Health Questionnaire-9, used in the Geng 2021 study to assess depressive symptoms among incarcerated men.</data>
      <data key="d3">0.86</data>
      <data key="d4">037d79c5-a241-4f38-8c08-cac6a4c5c0ff_chunk_31</data>
      <data key="d5">037d79c5-a241-4f38-8c08-cac6a4c5c0ff,5e787f6f-1547-4d32-aa5f-4a0f4d841129,41fb90c0-1594-48bd-b974-39b7d20799d4,af5ff8eb-8135-49d4-81fd-6de4008d60d8,d134d8d2-15f1-4ff0-8200-7d5648814a90,38ae95af-7b69-4f7b-a1f0-e672a8f6c0c1,46ccdeeb-683a-4650-9e07-68526b50880c,955321f0-cf24-4364-98c1-bbcf8dcd88cd,9959c1fe-4690-4814-83c8-bfd1da0c04bb,c25b6f4c-84d2-420a-96d3-e1e3b098131c,d4be01b0-0472-4ae9-a366-e27372d7422c,104e587b-e1a7-495c-92cb-cf76b7504b4c,49cf3a6d-f9ae-40b3-a69d-cb2b9c6b11ee,531dd921-3435-419e-b587-7dfeebb99084</data>
