      <data key="d0">GLOBAL COGNITIVE FUNCTIONING</data>
      <data key="d1">COGNITIVE_DOMAIN</data>
      <data key="d2">Global cognitive functioning refers to overall cognitive performance across multiple domains, including memory, attention, executive function, language, and visuospatial abilities. It is relevant because the Montreal Cognitive Assessment is cited as a tool for assessing cognition broadly. | Broad cognitive outcome targeted by the cognitive assessment battery. The excerpt describes assessment of overall cognitive functioning and cognitive impairment using screening instruments including ACE-III. | The cognitive outcome domain discussed in relation to mild cognitive impairment, conversion to dementia, and the need for early detection and intervention in older adults. | General cognitive performance domain implied by the use of neuropsychological tests.</data>
