etween COVID-19 and later cognitive impairment. | COVID-19 survivors were reported to have cognitive impairment, cognitive issues, or cognitive deficits, which were linked with PTSD symptoms and psychological distress. | Cognitive impairment is reported in COVID-19 survivors and following COVID-19 infection in cited studies. | The related article title identifies subjects as cognitively impaired after COVID-19, supporting an association between COVID-19 and cognitive impairment. The excerpt does not provide causality, effect size, timing, or severity stratification. | COVID-19 is discussed in studies examining correlates of cognitive impairment, although the excerpt does not establish definitive causality. | COVID-19 is associated with cognitive impairment, as indicated by the cited study title reporting cognitive impairment in the subacute stage of COVID-19. | A cited title reports cognitive impairment in chronic COVID-19 patients, supporting an association between COVID-19 and impaired cognition. The excerpt does not provide effect size, causality, or a specific cognitive subdomain. | The excerpt explicitly refers to COVID-19-related cognitive impairments, supporting an association between COVID-19 and impaired cognition. | The article title on factors associated with cognitive impairment in patients with persisting sequelae of COVID-19 supports a link between COVID-19 and post-infectious cognitive impairment.</data>
