      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">For anger control, the cool area is described as larger than the warm area, suggesting PCEs generally overcome ACEs. | PCEs had a statistically significant promotive effect on anger control. | PCEs were analyzed as influencing anger control as one of the separate mood challenge indicators. | PCEs strongly predicted anger control outcomes and more effectively offset ACE-related detriment for anger control. | Both males and females benefited from PCEs in relation to anger control.</data>
