      <data key="d8">OCCURRENCE OF INTRUSIVE MEMORIES</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Cognitive flexibility was included as a predictor of intrusive memory occurrence.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.7</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">ee75d849-2123-48c8-986c-64305968800f_chunk_34</data>
      <data key="d14">ee75d849-2123-48c8-986c-64305968800f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="SWITCHING STROOP">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">SWITCHING STROOP</data>
      <data key="d9">MEASURED_BY</data>
      <data key="d10">Cognitive flexibility is measured by Switching Stroop because the relevant dimension periodically switches between ink colour and text/word colour, requiring adaptation to changing rules.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.82</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">52c7de5e-fc25-4a5d-9923-173be2895317_chunk_19</data>
      <data key="d14">52c7de5e-fc25-4a5d-9923-173be2895317</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="TRAIL MAKING">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">TRAIL MAKING</data>
      <data key="d9">MEASURED_BY</data>
      <data key="d10">Cognitive flexibility is measured by the alternating Trail Making condition, which requires switching between numbers and letters while maintaining ascending order.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.84</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">52c7de5e-fc25-4a5d-9923-173be2895317_chunk_19</data>
      <data key="d14">52c7de5e-fc25-4a5d-9923-173be2895317</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="MALADAPTIVE COPING">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">MALADAPTIVE COPING</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Higher cognitive flexibility appeared to buffer the association between school-related stress exposure and maladaptive coping. | The study focused on whether cognitive flexibility has a protective role against maladaptive coping-related outcomes. | Cognitive flexibility moderated the level of maladaptive coping associated with stress exposure; the stress exposure–maladaptive coping association was stronger among those with lower cognitive flexibility. | Higher cognitive flexibility was associated with decreased maladaptive coping. | Cognitive flexibility influenced the association between stress exposure and maladaptive coping: the stress–coping association was present at low but not high levels of cognitive flexibility. | Lower cognitive flexibility is linked to greater risk of maladaptive coping, whereas enhancing cognitive flexibility is suggested to improve coping.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.87</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_0</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="SELF-REPORT QUESTIONNAIRES">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">SELF-REPORT QUESTIONNAIRES</data>
      <data key="d9">MEASURED_BY</data>
      <data key="d10">Cognitive flexibility was assessed using questionnaire-based measures.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.76</data>
      <data key="d12">3</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_0</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="PCS SYMPTOM SEVERITY">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">PTSD SYMPTOM SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">High cognitive flexibility is described as protective, weakening or eliminating the association between continuous stress exposure and PTSD symptom severity. | Higher cognitive flexibility is described as a protective factor that reduces PTSD symptom severity following traumatic incidents. | Cognitive flexibility is expected to play a moderating role in the association between school-related stress and PTSD symptoms. | Cognitive flexibility was included as a moderator, and the text reports a significant interaction between school-related stress exposure and cognitive flexibility in predicting PTSD symptom severity. | Cognitive flexibility is described as protective: high cognitive flexibility buffered the relationship between stress exposure and PTSD symptom severity, while low flexibility was associated with greater symptom severity under higher exposure. | Higher cognitive flexibility is described as protective, while lower cognitive flexibility is associated with higher risk of developing PTSD symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.88</data>
      <data key="d12">3</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_1</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="DEPRESSIVE SYMPTOM SEVERITY">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">DEPRESSION SYMPTOM SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Cognitive flexibility moderates the relationship between repeated traumatic exposure and depression symptoms; individuals with higher cognitive flexibility show no exposure-symptom association.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.72</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_10</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="SCHOOL-RELATED STRESS EXPOSURE">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">WORK-RELATED STRESS EXPOSURE</data>
      <data key="d9">MODULATED_BY_EXPOSURE</data>
      <data key="d10">The study measured cognitive flexibility alongside continuous work-related stress exposure, implying that cognitive flexibility was examined in relation to occupational stress exposure.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.45</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_16</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="PTSD SYMPTOMS">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">PTSD SYMPTOMS</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Cognitive flexibility is described as influencing clinical symptoms, including PTSD symptoms, and moderating the relationship between stress exposure and PTSD symptoms. | The cited article 'Cognitive flexibility predicts PTSD symptoms' indicates that cognitive flexibility is associated with or predictive of PTSD symptom levels.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.9</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_29</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="POST-TRAUMATIC STRESS DISORDER">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">POST-TRAUMATIC STRESS DISORDER</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">The cited literature links cognitive flexibility to PTSD symptoms, including its possible role in differentiating PTSD-related impairments from depression-related impairments.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.55</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_44</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="DEPRESSION">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">DEPRESSION</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">The cited literature links cognitive flexibility to depression symptoms through selective impairments that may help distinguish depression from PTSD.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.52</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57_chunk_44</data>
      <data key="d14">b1a08202-3b7d-4086-b35d-61754b0def57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY" target="ENCODING STRATEGIES">
      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE FLEXIBILITY</data>
      <data key="d8">COPING STRATEGIES</data>
      <data key="d9">MEDIATED_BY</data>
