      <data key="d10">Brain fog is presented as a named cognitive complaint within the broader topic of cognitive symptoms in chronic fatigue syndrome. Because the valid relationship set lacks a 'subtype_of' relation, COMPARED_TO is used to express the conceptual alignment between the specific symptom label and the broader cognitive-symptom domain. | Brain fog is presented as a cognitive complaint relevant to counseling and treatment of midlife women and overlaps with broader cognitive symptoms. | Brain fog is presented as an ambiguous term for cognitive symptoms whose underlying causes can vary.</data>
