    <edge source="EXECUTIVE FUNCTION" target="COVID-19">
      <data key="d7">EXECUTIVE FUNCTION</data>
      <data key="d8">COVID-19</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Executive function showed a strong association with lower risk of viral infections, especially COVID-19. | Poorer executive function was specifically associated with viral infection risk, with COVID-19 highlighted as a key example. | Lower baseline executive function was associated with future viral infections including COVID-19. | Because most incident viral infections were COVID-19, the association between poorer executive function and future viral infection risk largely reflects COVID-19 cases. | Executive function specifically predicted future viral infection risk, particularly COVID-19.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.9</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">f1a9ac9c-ad81-407f-9d35-d5d0b1f52702_chunk_3</data>
