      <data key="d8">CORTICAL EXCITABILITY</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Cortical excitability is one of the brain physiological aspects examined in relation to chronotype and time-of-day. | The study systematically investigated the modulatory impact of chronotype on cortical excitability in the human motor cortex. | Chronotype was part of significant interaction effects with daytime and TMS intensity on the slope of the input-output curve and MEP amplitudes. | The results indicated chronotype-specific variation in cortical excitability. | Chronotype is described as being associated with brain physiology, including daytime-dependent cortical excitability. | The text states that cortical excitability shows chronotype-specific modulation. | Chronotype is relevant for motor cortex functionality, including basic physiological functions such as cortical excitability. | Cortical excitability is described as strongly related to chronotype in humans. | The truncated cited title states that chronotype influences diurnal variations in excitability, supporting an effect of chronotype on excitability.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.94</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">d9e6bfa7-e0c7-4041-82d3-54049860c2bf_chunk_4</data>
