      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Neuroplasticity is one of the physiological aspects investigated for chronotype-related effects. | Chronotype is linked in the discussion to physiological brain measures including neuroplasticity, though the causal interpretation is limited by possible sleep-pressure confounding. | Neuroplasticity is described as strongly related to chronotype in humans, suggesting chronotype may influence plasticity-related outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.86</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">d9e6bfa7-e0c7-4041-82d3-54049860c2bf_chunk_4</data>
