      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Based on prior findings, the study predicts that LCov is associated with altered inter-network functional connectivity during the Stroop task. | LCov was associated with altered inter-network functional connectivity when compared with healthy controls, summarized by the section heading 'Impaired inter-network connectivity.' | LCov is associated with impaired inter-network functional connectivity involving frontal, lateral occipital, Language, Salience, and DMN-related regions. | LCov shows increased inter-network connectivity relative to healthy controls in salience, language, sensorimotor, and visual networks.</data>
