      <data key="d8">MILD COVID-19</data>
      <data key="d9">VARIES_WITH_SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d10">Frequent neurocognitive deficits were reported after recovery from mild COVID-19, linking the outcome to a mild disease-severity subgroup. | Neurocognitive deficits are referenced after recovery from mild COVID-19, indicating that such impairments can occur even in a mild severity category. | The cited evidence indicates that neurocognitive deficits can be observed after mild COVID-19, showing relevance across severity strata. | The neurocognitive deficits are specifically reported in the context of mild COVID-19. The text identifies the severity stratum but does not quantify differences across severity levels. | Neurocognitive deficits are reported specifically in the context of recovery from mild COVID-19. | Neurocognitive deficits were reported after recovery from mild COVID-19, showing that such deficits can be observed even following non-severe disease. | Neurocognitive deficits are specifically reported after recovery from mild COVID-19. | The reported post-recovery neurocognitive deficits are specifically described in the context of mild COVID-19.</data>
