      <data key="d8">FATIGUE</data>
      <data key="d9">CONFOUNDED_BY</data>
      <data key="d10">Fatigue was tracked alongside cognitive outcomes and may influence cognitive performance or perceived cognitive impairment in PCS patients. | Fatigue is a common Post-COVID Syndrome symptom that may influence cognitive complaints or psychometric performance. | Fatigue is listed as a related factor in the examination of cognitive function in post-COVID syndrome, and may influence cognitive performance or its interpretation. | Fatigue co-occurs with cognitive dysfunction after mild COVID-19 and may complicate interpretation of post-infectious cognitive complaints. | Fatigue is reported alongside cognitive dysfunction after mild COVID-19 and may influence cognitive complaints or performance, making it a potential confounding factor. | Fatigue was assessed as a factor that may influence changes in cognitive scores over time and could contribute to measured or perceived post-COVID cognitive impairment. | Fatigue is collected as a factor that may affect cognitive functioning and complicate attribution of cognitive differences solely to PCC.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.76</data>
