      <data key="d8">NON-HOSPITALIZED COVID-19</data>
      <data key="d9">VARIES_WITH_SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d10">Persistent cognitive dysfunction is specifically reported in non-hospitalized COVID-19 long haulers, showing that cognitive impairment was documented in a non-hospitalized subgroup. | Cognitive dysfunction is reported in non-hospitalized COVID-19 long-haulers, indicating that impairment is not limited to hospitalized patients. | Cognitive dysfunction is reported specifically in non-hospitalized COVID-19 long haulers, indicating that post-COVID cognitive problems are not limited to hospitalized or severe acute disease. | The Graham et al. citation specifically reports cognitive dysfunction in non-hospitalized COVID-19 patients. This indicates that cognitive dysfunction can occur even in a non-hospitalized, relatively less severe acute disease subgroup, although the excerpt does not provide a direct severity comparison.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.78</data>
