      <data key="d8">POST-ACUTE COVID-19 SYNDROME</data>
      <data key="d9">PERSISTS_AT</data>
      <data key="d10">The review notes that common neuropsychological difficulties may be a feature of post-acute COVID-19 syndrome and calls for assessment of the long-term course of cognitive deficits. | Persistent cognitive dysfunction in COVID-19 long haulers is conceptually aligned with the post-acute COVID-19 syndrome phase mentioned in the reference list, although the excerpt does not provide a specific duration or cognitive measurement for PCS.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.82</data>
