      <data key="d7">COGNITIVE DYSFUNCTION</data>
      <data key="d8">PSYCHIATRIC DISTRESS</data>
      <data key="d9">CONFOUNDED_BY</data>
      <data key="d10">Psychiatric distress may contribute to subjective cognitive complaints or affect performance in domains such as attention and memory, complicating interpretation of post-COVID cognitive dysfunction. | Because psychiatric distress is reported alongside cognitive dysfunction after COVID-19 and can influence cognitive performance or symptom reporting, it is a plausible confounding factor for interpreting post-COVID cognitive dysfunction. | Psychiatric distress is mentioned alongside cognitive dysfunction after COVID-19 and may influence cognitive symptoms or their interpretation. | Psychiatric distress is listed alongside cognitive dysfunction and may confound or modify interpretation of cognitive complaints after COVID-19. | Psychiatric distress is co-reported with cognitive dysfunction after COVID-19 and may independently influence cognitive complaints or test performance.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.72</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">63b31c15-b9bb-4a8e-a6dd-082b7c1908fa_chunk_5</data>
