      <data key="d8">LONG-TERM FOLLOW-UP</data>
      <data key="d9">PERSISTS_AT</data>
      <data key="d10">The collection of cited studies on post-COVID outcomes supports evaluation of cognitive dysfunction beyond the acute infection period, although the snippet does not specify a precise duration for cognitive persistence. | The study did not determine whether cognitive outcomes persist at longer-term follow-up; the authors recommended future research to assess outcomes beyond 3–6 months. | The excerpt places COVID-19 outcomes in a post-infection and long-term outcomes context, although the specific cognitive-dysfunction citation does not provide an exact follow-up interval.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.62</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">63b31c15-b9bb-4a8e-a6dd-082b7c1908fa_chunk_5</data>
