      <data key="d9">VARIES_WITH_SEVERITY</data>
      <data key="d10">Studies assess cognitive function in people with mild cognitive impairment as a less severe cognitive impairment state. | Cognitive functions are considered in the context of mild cognitive impairment, representing a less severe level of cognitive decline. | The study population is older adults with mild cognitive impairment, indicating that cognitive function is examined within a mild impairment severity context.</data>
