      <data key="d8">SOCIAL NETWORK</data>
      <data key="d9">CONFOUNDED_BY</data>
      <data key="d10">Social network is identified as a protective factor that may influence subjective cognitive functioning and help explain variation across pandemic phases. | Social network is identified as a potential protective or vulnerability factor and may affect subjective cognitive functioning through psychosocial support or isolation. | Social network was included as a covariate and potential protective or vulnerability factor in the analysis of change over time. | Social network was included as a covariate and protective or vulnerability-related factor, indicating that social connectedness was considered when modeling subjective cognitive functioning. | Temporal changes in subjective cognitive functioning varied by social network level, a psychosocial protective or vulnerability factor.</data>
      <data key="d11">0.78</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">9ac1c295-0116-47ef-a0b9-9e8531f02406_chunk_10</data>
