      <data key="d8">PERCEPTION</data>
      <data key="d9">AFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d10">Predictive processing posits that perception is shaped by predictions generated before actual stimulus exposure. | Predictive processing proposes that perception is actively shaped by the brain's predictions and interpretive mechanisms. | Predictive processing proposes that perception is constructed through active hypothesis testing and model generation. | Predictive processing accounts for the dynamic and interactive nature of perception through prediction and feedback. | Predictive processing accounts for perception through mechanisms involving prediction and top-down modulation. | Predictive processing is described as a model of perception whose neurophysiological evidence is evaluated.</data>
