      <data key="d9">MEDIATED_BY</data>
      <data key="d10">The cited Delgado-Alonso et al. study found that fatigue played a central role as the main mediator linking objective cognition and subjective cognitive complaints. | Fatigue is assessed in relation to subjective cognitive complaints and may influence the severity or interpretation of self-reported cognitive problems in post-COVID syndrome. | Fatigue is examined in relation to subjective cognitive complaints and may contribute to or partially explain perceived cognitive problems. | Fatigue may confound subjective cognitive complaints, as higher fatigue burden can contribute to perceived cognitive difficulty independently of objective cognitive impairment.</data>
